{"id":"15.4.2","doc":"T","title":"Split Peripheral Regions into Split Regions","words":308,"blocks":[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":1,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Each of ESP32-S3's peripheral region can be further split into 11 regions (from Peri Region0 ~ Peri Region10) for more flexible permission control."}]}]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":2,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"For example, the registers for ESP32-S3's "},{"t":"block","v":"GDMA","id":"gdma"},{"t":"text","v":" controller are allocated as:"}]}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":3,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"5 sets of registers for 5 of each RX channel"}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":4,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"5 sets of registers for 5 of each TX channel"}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":5,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"1 set of registers for configuration"}]}]}]]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":6,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"As seen above, GDMA's peripheral region is divided into 11 split regions (implemented in hardware), which can be configured with different permission independently, thus achieving independent permission control to each GDMA channel."}]}]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":7,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Users can configure CPU's read (R) and write (W) accesses to a specific split region (Peri Region n) from the Secure World and the Non-secure World by configuring PMS_CORE_m_Region_PMS_CONSTRAN_n_REG."}]},{"n":8,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Note that permission can be configured independently for CPU0 and CPU1."}]}]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":9,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Notes on PMS_CORE_m_Region_PMS_CONSTRAN_n_REG:"}]}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":10,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"m can be 0 or 1 for CPU0 and CPU1 respectively."}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":11,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"n can be 1~14, in which"}]}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":12,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Region_PMS_CONSTRAN_1_REG is for configuring CPU's permission from the Secure World."}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":13,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Region_PMS_CONSTRAN_2_REG is for configuring CPU's permission from the Non-secure World."}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":14,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Region_PMS_CONSTRAN_n_REG (n = 3~14) are used to configuring the starting addresses for each Peri Regions."}]},{"n":15,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Note the starting address of each Peri Region is also the ending address of the previous Peri Region."}]}]}]]}]]},{"t":"table","caption":"Table 15.4-2. Access Configuration of Peri Regions","head":[[{"t":"text","v":"Peri Regions"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Starting Address Configuration"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Access Configuration, Secure World"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Access Configuration, Non-secure World"}]],"rows":[{"n":16,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"Peri Region0"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Region_PMS_CONSTRAN_3_REG"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Region_PMS_CONSTRAN_1_REG [1:0]"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Region_PMS_CONSTRAN_2_REG [1:0]"}]]},{"n":17,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"Peri Region1"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Region_PMS_CONSTRAN_4_REG"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Region_PMS_CONSTRAN_1_REG [3:2]"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Region_PMS_CONSTRAN_2_REG [3:2]"}]]},{"n":18,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"Peri Region2"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Region_PMS_CONSTRAN_5_REG"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Region_PMS_CONSTRAN_1_REG [5:4]"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Region_PMS_CONSTRAN_2_REG [5:4]"}]]},{"n":19,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"Peri Region3"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Region_PMS_CONSTRAN_6_REG"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Region_PMS_CONSTRAN_1_REG [7:6]"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Region_PMS_CONSTRAN_2_REG [7:6]"}]]},{"n":20,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"Peri Region4"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Region_PMS_CONSTRAN_7_REG"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Region_PMS_CONSTRAN_1_REG [9:8]"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Region_PMS_CONSTRAN_2_REG [9:8]"}]]},{"n":21,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"Peri Region5"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Region_PMS_CONSTRAN_8_REG"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Region_PMS_CONSTRAN_1_REG [11:10]"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Region_PMS_CONSTRAN_2_REG [11:10]"}]]},{"n":22,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"Peri Region6"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Region_PMS_CONSTRAN_9_REG"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Region_PMS_CONSTRAN_1_